  "sources_described": "All water is San Francisco Regional Water System (SFPUC) surface water stored in reservoirs in the Sierra Nevada (Hetch Hetchy, unfiltered but UV/chlorine disinfected, pH adjusted, fluoridated and chloraminated), Alameda County and San Mateo County; local Alameda County reservoir water is treated at the Sunol Valley Water Treatment Plant. In 2025 neither the SFRWS upcountry non-Hetch Hetchy sources nor its groundwater wells were used, but the SFRWS imported a very small amount (0.38%) of treated water from Valley Water in April and May (page 8).",
