  "violations": [
    "Page 4, 'Notification of Process Monitoring Violation': the SFRWS failed to monitor for recycled filter backwash water turbidity at its Sunol Valley Water Treatment Plant from June 23, 2025 to July 2, 2025. The monitoring violation was the result of equipment failure and was corrected on July 3, 2025; it was not an emergency and did not impact water quality.",
    "Page 2: '100% Compliance with drinking water standards'. Table footnote 1 (page 7): 'All results met State and Federal drinking water health standards.'"
  ],
  "extraction_notes": "Tables on pages 6-7 are 'detected contaminants' only (single system-wide set of values, no per-source columns). The TURBIDITY section is split by source as rows (Unfiltered Hetch Hetchy Water; Filtered Water from SVWTP), so those entries carry the row label in source_group; all other entries have source_group null. Most values are SFPUC regional system results; lead/copper are PHWD tap samples from September 2023 (footnotes 6-7) and the next LCR round is 2026. Two extra entries are not table rows: treated-water fluoride from footnote 4 and the 'No PFAS Detected' statement from page 4. Convention: a range printed 'ND - x' or '<n - x' is stored range_low 0 / range_high x (the printed string is kept in notes). Rows whose Average (or 90th percentile) is printed 'ND' or '<n' but whose range shows a detection are stored value null, average null, detected true, value_basis 'average (printed ND)' - nothing is substituted for the unprintable average. Rows printed ND with no range are detected false. 'sample_year' is the latest year when the report prints a year range; the printed range is in notes."
}
